@@ -0,0 +1,64 @@
+# GBM Platform
+
+GBM owns **login, logout, session/JWT, filters, and user management**. Scheme modules such as PPF are separate Spring Boot apps.
+
+## Flow
+
+1. Browser opens GBM on port **8081**.
+2. User logs in. GBM returns a **JWT**.
+3. GBM Home lists modules (PPF first).
+4. Opening PPF sends the **same JWT** to PPF on port **8082**.
+5. PPF does **not** log the user in again. It only verifies the token.
+
+```
+Browser
+  ├─ /api/auth/*, /api/home  →  GBM  :8081
+  └─ /api/ppf/*              →  PPF  :8082   (Authorization: Bearer <jwt>)
+```
+
+Both apps must use the same `GBM_TOKEN_SECRET`.
+
+## Run locally (H2, no Oracle)
+
+Terminal 1:
+
+```bash
+./mvnw spring-boot:run -Dspring-boot.run.profiles=h2
+```
+
+Demo user (H2 profile only): `admin.ppf` / `Admin@123456`
+
+Then start [PPF](https://github.com/autidnyanesh/PPF) with the same secret and profile `h2`.
+
+Open http://localhost:8081
+
+## Oracle
+
+```bash
+export GBM_DB_URL=jdbc:oracle:thin:@localhost:1521:xe
+export GBM_DB_USERNAME=...
+export GBM_DB_PASSWORD=...
+export GBM_TOKEN_SECRET=change-me-to-a-long-shared-secret-32b
+./mvnw spring-boot:run
+```
+
+Optional table script: `src/main/resources/db/schema-oracle.sql`
+
+First admin (once):
+
+```bash
+curl -X POST http://localhost:8081/api/auth/bootstrap \
+  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
+  -d '{"username":"admin.ppf","password":"Admin@123456","displayName":"GBM Admin"}'
+```
+
+## API
+
+| Method | Path | Auth |
+|---|---|---|
+| POST | `/api/auth/bootstrap` | public, first user only |
+| POST | `/api/auth/login` | public |
+| POST | `/api/auth/logout` | JWT |
+| GET | `/api/auth/me` | JWT |
+| GET/POST/PATCH/DELETE | `/api/auth/users` | JWT + ADMIN |
+| GET | `/api/home` | JWT |
